  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Justice and Peace national desk</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is intended for capacity building and builds trust among the Churches, Religious/community leaders and communities in northern Sudan. 

During 21 years of civil war in south Sudan, SCC was divided into two: SCC proper in the north or government controlled areas and NSCC in the south or SPLA controlled areas.  This means relationships were destroyed by the war and must be rebuilt and sustained, underlying issues that caused the longest running conflict in Africa must be addressed and community based systems that promote dialogue and consensus must be build.  

This project is meant to prepare a ground for dialogue on these issues.  Three workshops will be organized on; Peaceful Co-existence and unity in diversity, Peace Building and Conflict Transformation and Good governance.

Workshop participants will include Church Leaders, Local community Leaders (Chiefs), Women, Youth, and Local Authority Leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
